    <time>2024-08-04T20:01:47Z</time>
  </metadata>
  <wpt lat="46.53356552417898" lon="-70.78726866071175">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who want an easier ride from here can take this  route that bypasses Massif park. Majority is on paved rail trail. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.77478469244251" lon="-66.61714307512288">
    <name>Big Climb</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Some very rugged climbing miles ahead. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.56986211999189" lon="-67.67190823394522">
    <name>Limited Services</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>There are very few services for next 220km until you reach Murdochville</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.95094475496267" lon="-65.49401188945329">
    <name>No Services</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>No services for next 100km to Gaspe</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.56182995208534" lon="-67.68582180829992">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who want to bypass the Gaspesie Penninsula ride can take this quicker route to New Brunswick </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.12154848857872" lon="-66.31168662543344">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can cut through on this road for a shortcut</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.400159682654504" lon="-69.67209710106435">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to stay on rail trail here.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="47.09331764361799" lon="-69.97883659402794">
    <name>Limited services for next 100km</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.57496491138905" lon="-67.66851624895614">
    <name>Gaspesie Penninsula</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Expect some rugged terrain ahead and challenging riding. Riders will need to be self sufficient in places. Water not always available.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.71234000000002" lon="-66.88572">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who want a less rugged route from here can take this bypass up to the St. Lawrence River. A combo of good dirt road riding and pavement. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.93860363045249" lon="-66.11818729748816">
    <name>Possible logging trucks on this road</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Road can also be dusty. More so with heavier RV traffic.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.336200000000005" lon="-68.29038999999999">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to stay on main road (Hwy 234) going north east to meet up with the route further along.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.52738034765662" lon="-67.91345724607164">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to stay on main road here</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.93794256598932" lon="-66.11985298886094">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders who need to shorten the route can take this main road (hwy 299) south to meet up with the route further along the peninsula. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.871725211592754" lon="-65.28642276364899">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>It is possible for riders to take the paved hwy all the way to Gaspe. Road may lack shoulder. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.763734761035096" lon="-65.09416895210784">
    <name>Landslide area</name>
    <cmt>caution</cmt>
    <desc>Remnants of landslide may make require a bit of hike-a-bike. But nothing too arduous. </desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>danger</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.07367313622761" lon="-65.49763902338283">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can also choose to take this paved road going west</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.63356896620445" lon="-67.2019555069446">
    <name>Route Alternative</name>
    <cmt>control</cmt>
    <desc>Riders can choose to stay on more established main road here instead of less maintained road along the river.</desc>
    <sym>Dot</sym>
    <type>checkpoint</type>
  </wpt>
  <wpt lat="48.61724453973247" lon="-64.27372075691493">
    <name>Railway tracks</name>
